## Part 3: Writing and Graphing Linear Equations

In this section, you will master writing linear equations in slope-intercept form ($y = mx + b$) and graphing them on the coordinate plane. Ensure all algebraic steps are shown clearly for full credit.

> **Key Concept: Slope-Intercept Form**  
> The equation of a line is most commonly written as:  
> $$y = mx + b$$  
> Where:  
> * **$m$** is the **slope** (rate of change).  
> * **$b$** is the **y-intercept** (initial value at $x = 0$).

